              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a dressing forceps, a grasping instrument commonly used to handle gauze, swabs and dressing materials during wound care and minor surgical procedures. It usually has spring-action arms and opposed tips, which may be plain, serrated or toothed depending on the pattern. It is used for wound dressing, wound cleaning and selected superficial tissue-handling procedures. Complications of improper use include tissue trauma, bleeding and wound contamination. Before use, I would inspect the tips, spring tension, alignment, cleanliness and sterility.”"
                }
              ]
